  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Completing the square reveals a lower bound:\n\\[\nf(x)=x^2-2x=(x-1)^2-1\\ge -1.\n\\]\nEquality holds at \\(x=1\\), which belongs to \\([0,3]\\). Therefore the minimum value is \\(-1\\).",
